!!id:"https://tson.io/2026/32/ltr8/cli/diagnostics-6.tn"
!!meta:"https://tson.io/2026/32/m/meta.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/32/m/core.tn"
@doc:"""
  This project's own schema !!id convention (see CLAUDE.md's "Project-owned schema !!id
  convention"): /2026/32 is the spec revision this schema is written against, ltr8 is the
  publishing org, cli is this module's own schema group, and the trailing -6 is this schema's
  own version -- bumped when file_report/validation_run were added, so `validate` can name the
  file each verdict belongs to inside one document; when the fields that may have nothing to
  say became optional rather than empty; when path/schema_pointer joined them, DUPLICATE_FIELD
  having been missing from diagnostic_code all along; and when FIELD_FIXED joined that same
  enum. Per that same convention's "bump it, under a new name" rule, never edit a published
  schema's own content in place.
  """
{
  diagnostic_code => !enum [
    FIELD_REQUIRED FIELD_FIXED TYPE_MISMATCH WRONG_ARITY UNKNOWN_TYPE_REF ATOM_CONSTRAINT_VIOLATION
    UNRECOGNIZED_FIELD DUPLICATE_MAP_KEY DUPLICATE_FIELD SCHEMA_ERROR UNKNOWN_TYPE VALIDATION_ERROR
  ]
  @doc:"""
    One problem, located at up to two ends: the value in the data (path, data_position) and the rule
    in the schema (schema_id, schema_pointer, schema_position). Either end may be absent -- a problem
    found in a schema has no data, and a schemaless read has no schema.

    Absence is written as absence: every field that may have nothing to say is optional here and
    renders as null in --output json. That includes both RFC 6901 pointers, and the distinction they
    draw is load-bearing: a present "" is the root, which a document-level schema problem genuinely
    carries, while null means this diagnostic has no such end at all.

    A position is "line:column:byte_offset", all three 1-based except byte_offset, which counts
    UTF-8 bytes from 0 ([TSON-DATA] §8.1).
    """
  diagnostic => {
    path: text?
    schema_pointer: text?
    schema_id: text?
    code: diagnostic_code
    message: text
    expected: text?
    actual: text?
    data_position: text?
    schema_position: text?
  }
  validation_report => { valid: boolean  errors: [diagnostic] }
  file_report => { file: text  valid: boolean  errors: [diagnostic] }
  validation_run => { valid: boolean  files: [file_report]  errors: [diagnostic] }
}
